This dialog shows overlay \b BadPixels' map\b0  <automatic>. Shows & edits overlay \b BadPixels' map manual\b0 .\par
\par
At open this dialog:\par
= <\cf1 by current loaded image\cf0 > assigns overlay's dimension,\par
= <\cf1 tries to\cf0 > loads the overlays from SDK-specific location.\par
= displays status line :\line   ~ e.g. "\cf1 BMP NNNNN pixels, BPMM doesn't exist\cf0 ",\par
  ~ e.g. "\cf1 BMP doesn't exist, BPMM MMMMN pixels\cf0 ".\par
\f2\fs18\par
Editing area (\cf1 marked by green \cf3\highlight6 color\cf1\highlight0  in UI-topology\cf0 ):\par
- BPMM_org\tab two spin_edits (\cf1 x & y\cf0 ) specify 2D-point;\par
- BPMM_cnt\tab combo_box & spin_edit specify direction & count.\par
\par
The actions:\par
[Browse]      \tab selects location of loading overlays;\par
[:= XY]       \tab BPMM_org := Marker_XY;\par
[XY :=]       \tab Marker_XY := BPMM_org;\par
[count :=]    \tab assigns BPMM_cnt by Marker_XY;\par
[:= whole Row]\tab assigns BPMM_org, BPMM_cnt by Marker_XY;\par
[:= whole Col]\tab -"-;\par
[Load]        \tab loads the overlays (\cf1 abandons changes\cf0 );\par
[Save]        \tab saves BPMM in file;\par
[Erase]       \tab fills BPMM by 0 (\cf1 [Erase]+[Save] delete BPMM.raw\cf0 );\par
[Mark]        \tab fills editing area by 1;\par
[Clean]       \tab fills editing area by 0.\par
\f0\fs20\par
Pixels' colors and text-background:\line\f2\fs18 - dark magenta \lang1042  \cf3\highlight12\b\lang1033 color\cf0\highlight0\b0  -\tab <>0 in BPM,\par
- light magenta \cf3\highlight13 color\cf0\highlight0  -\tab <>0 in BPMM,\line - green         \cf3\highlight6 color\cf0\highlight0  -\tab within "editing area".\line\par
\f0\fs20 To enhance visibility of ~pixel-size-details on specific monitor:\line   - utilize \ul GDI-stretch selection\ulnone  ~= "\i White|Black details\i0 " in the pop-up menu (\cf1 perhaps prefer GDI-build against GPU-build\cf0 );\line   - adjust "base bk-color" in [Settings]. \f2\par
